WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.793 --> 00:00:03.044
If you've ever wanted to know

00:00:03.044 --> 00:00:05.005
what a revolution looks like,

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:06.881
feast your eyes on Manila tonight.

00:00:09.592 --> 00:00:12.345
Marcos's regime ended in 1986

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:14.472
when he was toppled by what is now known

00:00:14.472 --> 00:00:16.975
as the People Power Revolution.

00:00:16.975 --> 00:00:19.644
The Filipino government has estimated

00:00:19.644 --> 00:00:23.815
that the amount the Marcos family pilfered

00:00:23.815 --> 00:00:26.484
was between $5 billion and $10 billion.

00:00:28.236 --> 00:00:29.320
So this is just graft

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:32.282
on an absolutely massive unheard of scale.

00:00:32.282 --> 00:00:35.368
Marcos declared martial law in 1972,

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:37.537
closed newspapers, jailed political foes,

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:39.456
turned parliament into a rubber stamp.

00:00:41.833 --> 00:00:45.503
The Marcos regime was very
concerned about dissidence,

00:00:45.503 --> 00:00:48.173
so the security forces are tasked

00:00:48.173 --> 00:00:50.592
with arresting the dissidents,

00:00:50.592 --> 00:00:53.011
torturing them for information.

00:00:53.011 --> 00:00:57.182
Oftentimes, the victim
would be summarily executed.

00:00:58.058 --> 00:00:59.976
A nation took to the streets tonight

00:00:59.976 --> 00:01:01.895
to celebrate its victory.

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:05.690
A dictator had fallen. The
people conquered his palace.

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:07.817
Reagan, who was president at this time,

00:01:07.817 --> 00:01:11.988
actually offered Marcos asylum in the U.S.

00:01:11.988 --> 00:01:14.824
And so when Marcos did ultimately decide

00:01:14.824 --> 00:01:17.577
to step down in February of 1986,

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:20.789
Reagan sent two planes to cart Marcos

00:01:20.789 --> 00:01:23.124
and 90 members of his entourage,

00:01:23.124 --> 00:01:25.919
along with millions of
dollars worth of loot.

00:01:27.128 --> 00:01:29.297
It is time to come to an understanding

00:01:29.297 --> 00:01:31.466
with both the government and Marcoses

00:01:31.466 --> 00:01:34.010
to compensate the human rights victims.

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:39.015
In 1992, after years of building the case,

00:01:40.308 --> 00:01:44.062
the Marcos class action
finally went to trial.

00:01:44.062 --> 00:01:49.067
The jury in Hawaii ultimately
held Marcos responsible.

00:01:50.985 --> 00:01:54.405
The judgment in total
was almost $2 billion,

00:01:54.405 --> 00:01:57.408
which was astronomical.

00:01:57.408 --> 00:01:59.327
It's been a long fight to this point,

00:01:59.327 --> 00:02:02.455
but we're going to continue
to fight to the end.

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:03.998
We knew at the outset that it

00:02:03.998 --> 00:02:08.128
was gonna be a very risky litigation.

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:10.463
At that point, what they
had was just a number

00:02:10.463 --> 00:02:15.301
on a piece of paper and
actually turning it into money

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:19.389
for the class was gonna be
a much harder challenge.

00:02:29.941 --> 00:02:31.776
My name is Haley Cohen Gilliland,

00:02:31.776 --> 00:02:36.030
and I am an independent
journalist based in Los Angeles.

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:39.868
We cannot succeed without
the support of our people.

00:02:39.868 --> 00:02:43.997
So Ferdinand Marcos ran the
Philippines for 21 years,

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:47.917
and he first blazed into
the presidency in 1965.

00:02:49.878 --> 00:02:52.380
He was a remarkably charismatic figure.

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:54.424
He was a wonderful orator.

00:02:54.424 --> 00:02:56.843
He had a beautiful wife
who was very elegant

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:59.345
and had a gorgeous singing voice,

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:03.725
and she would regale crowds
at his campaign rallies.

00:03:03.725 --> 00:03:07.312
Now everybody seems to be involved

00:03:07.312 --> 00:03:09.606
in the destiny not only of himself

00:03:09.606 --> 00:03:11.816
but of the entire content
of the entire nation,

00:03:11.816 --> 00:03:15.987
and this is what we have
been hoping and praying for.

00:03:15.987 --> 00:03:17.697
His first term was really promising.

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:21.618
He invested really
widely in infrastructure

00:03:21.618 --> 00:03:25.205
and urban beautification and
especially rural development,

00:03:25.205 --> 00:03:27.874
and so his base of
followers grew and grew.

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:30.001
Then in his second term,

00:03:30.001 --> 00:03:32.045
he started to run into some problems,

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:35.340
allegations of corruption,
growing poverty,

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:40.345
and simultaneously, some
separatist guerrilla groups,

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:43.514
violent groups, started
to pop up in the country.

00:03:43.514 --> 00:03:46.351
Ferdinand Marcos at this
point takes advantage

00:03:46.351 --> 00:03:51.356
of the advent of these
groups to declare martial law

00:03:51.606 --> 00:03:55.318
and essentially rule
the country by decree.

00:03:55.318 --> 00:03:57.028
I have received hundreds and hundreds

00:03:57.028 --> 00:04:00.448
of telegrams from all
corners of the Philippines,

00:04:00.448 --> 00:04:04.452
congratulating you and incidentally me

00:04:04.452 --> 00:04:07.580
for the proclamation of martial law.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:11.167
And all the while Filipino citizens

00:04:11.167 --> 00:04:13.503
were being tortured and imprisoned,

00:04:13.503 --> 00:04:17.840
the Marcoses would spend
really brazenly and lavishly.

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:21.803
So they amassed dozens
of luxury properties all

00:04:21.803 --> 00:04:24.639
over the Philippines and around the world.

00:04:24.639 --> 00:04:29.644
Then in 1986, Ferdinand Marcos
decided to call an election.

00:04:29.852 --> 00:04:31.688
Marcos! Marcos!

00:04:31.688 --> 00:04:34.691
By all accounts, Marcos
fixed that election,

00:04:34.691 --> 00:04:36.317
and when that became clear,

00:04:36.317 --> 00:04:39.320
that unleashed massive
protests around the country.

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:42.365
Millions of Filipinos
flooded into the streets,

00:04:42.365 --> 00:04:44.492
demanding that Marcos step down.

00:04:44.492 --> 00:04:46.286
And ultimately in that case,

00:04:46.286 --> 00:04:49.455
the U.S. finally said, "Enough is enough,"

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:52.292
and encouraged Marcos
to step down as well.

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:55.795
But they didn't completely
cut support because Reagan,

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:57.505
who was president at this time,

00:04:57.505 --> 00:05:01.843
actually offered Marcos asylum in the U.S.

00:05:01.843 --> 00:05:04.637
And so when Marcos did ultimately decide

00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:07.390
to step down in February of 1986,

00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:10.601
Reagan sent two planes to cart Marcos

00:05:10.601 --> 00:05:12.937
and 90 members of his entourage,

00:05:12.937 --> 00:05:15.815
along with millions of
dollars worth of loot,

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:17.567
diamonds and cash,

00:05:17.567 --> 00:05:20.486
some of which they carried
out in diaper boxes.

00:05:21.404 --> 00:05:26.409
Reagan sent planes to cart
those people and assets

00:05:26.701 --> 00:05:30.371
to Honolulu where Marcos
was welcomed with asylum.

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:39.339
My name's Robert Swift.

00:05:39.339 --> 00:05:42.842
Most people call me Bob. I'm a litigator.

00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:44.635
I do complex litigation,

00:05:44.635 --> 00:05:47.680
and I've been doing that
for almost 48 years.

00:05:50.808 --> 00:05:54.604
At the time of the revolution
in the Philippines,

00:05:54.604 --> 00:05:57.523
there was a great deal
of publicity as well

00:05:57.523 --> 00:06:02.070
as information that
various human rights groups

00:06:02.070 --> 00:06:06.407
have collected about human
rights abuses committed

00:06:06.407 --> 00:06:08.409
by the Marcos regime.

00:06:08.409 --> 00:06:13.331
And my initial intention was
to bring individual cases,

00:06:13.331 --> 00:06:18.211
but when I learned of the
enormity of the abuses,

00:06:19.087 --> 00:06:21.964
I decided that it was worthwhile

00:06:21.964 --> 00:06:24.175
to try bringing a class action.

00:06:24.175 --> 00:06:25.343
And the way that he did that

00:06:25.343 --> 00:06:28.471
was using this very rarely used statute

00:06:28.471 --> 00:06:31.015
called the Alien Tort Statute,

00:06:31.015 --> 00:06:36.020
and that statute was
first enacted in 1789.

00:06:36.104 --> 00:06:37.730
It's only a couple of sentences,

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:42.735
but it essentially allows
non-U.S. citizens to sue people

00:06:43.236 --> 00:06:47.490
for violations of
international law in U.S. court.

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:51.536
About 10,000 Filipino people signed on

00:06:51.536 --> 00:06:53.496
to become a part of this class action,

00:06:53.496 --> 00:06:55.998
which is absolutely a massive class.

00:06:55.998 --> 00:06:58.960
It is time to compensate
the human rights victims.

00:07:00.294 --> 00:07:05.091
The first named plaintiff
was a college-age girl

00:07:05.091 --> 00:07:08.052
by the name of Lilioso Hilao.

00:07:08.052 --> 00:07:14.475
She had written some
articles in the student press

00:07:14.475 --> 00:07:18.938
which were not flattering to the Marcoses

00:07:18.938 --> 00:07:20.940
or the Marcos regime.

00:07:21.983 --> 00:07:25.403
She was arrested by military,

00:07:25.403 --> 00:07:28.030
taken to a military detention center

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:30.616
where she was interrogated.

00:07:30.616 --> 00:07:32.243
When she was uncooperative,

00:07:32.243 --> 00:07:36.080
the military poured muriatic
acid down her throat,

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:38.458
and she died from asphyxiation.

00:07:42.879 --> 00:07:45.256
Another example is an individual

00:07:45.256 --> 00:07:47.300
by the name of Mariano Pimentel.

00:07:48.426 --> 00:07:52.180
Pimentel had been a
political leader in Mindanao.

00:07:52.180 --> 00:07:55.016
He'd been arrested several times.

00:07:55.016 --> 00:07:58.352
He was finally released from detention

00:07:58.352 --> 00:08:02.482
after more than six months,

00:08:02.482 --> 00:08:06.986
and on his way back to his province,

00:08:08.321 --> 00:08:11.282
military members in a Jeep stopped him,

00:08:11.282 --> 00:08:15.703
took him to a sugarcane
field, had him dig a grave.

00:08:15.703 --> 00:08:18.247
They then buried him up to his neck,

00:08:18.247 --> 00:08:22.960
and before they filled in the soil,

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:25.505
they broke a leg and broke an arm

00:08:25.505 --> 00:08:27.924
so that he wouldn't be
able to dig himself out.

00:08:27.924 --> 00:08:32.929
They then put the soil back in
and buried him up to his neck

00:08:34.055 --> 00:08:37.141
and they figured they would
let the ants do the rest.

00:08:37.141 --> 00:08:39.894
He survived because there
were several children

00:08:39.894 --> 00:08:42.563
who had been hiding in the sugarcane field

00:08:42.563 --> 00:08:47.360
who saw him and dug him
out, and he later emigrated

00:08:47.360 --> 00:08:49.237
to the United States where I met him.

00:09:02.959 --> 00:09:06.087
In addition, the present
state has the duty

00:09:06.087 --> 00:09:09.632
to uphold the need to
recompense its own victims.

00:09:11.175 --> 00:09:16.681
In 1992, after years of building the case,

00:09:16.681 --> 00:09:22.728
the Marcos class action finally
went to trial in Hawaii,

00:09:22.728 --> 00:09:29.986
and the jury in Hawaii ultimately
held Marcos responsible

00:09:29.986 --> 00:09:32.655
for the abuses and torture

00:09:32.655 --> 00:09:34.574
that had occurred under his regime.

00:09:37.827 --> 00:09:43.332
So in 1994, Swift asked
the jury for $1 billion,

00:09:43.332 --> 00:09:46.752
which represented $100,000 per victim,

00:09:46.752 --> 00:09:48.796
which he felt was appropriate amount.

00:09:48.796 --> 00:09:53.092
Well, I don't know that no other lawyer

00:09:53.092 --> 00:09:56.053
had ever asked a jury
for a billion dollars.

00:09:56.053 --> 00:09:58.139
However, our case is unique

00:09:58.139 --> 00:10:00.975
in that we really supported that number

00:10:00.975 --> 00:10:04.270
through the enormity of the
abuses that had occurred.

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:08.441
And the amount that the
jury ultimately awarded

00:10:08.441 --> 00:10:12.445
to the Marcos class
totaled almost two billion.

00:10:12.445 --> 00:10:14.822
That was astronomical figure,

00:10:14.822 --> 00:10:16.532
an absolutely unheard of figure.

00:10:16.532 --> 00:10:20.870
It was the largest ever personal
injury judgment in history.

00:10:23.873 --> 00:10:28.753
So immediately upon receiving
the monetary judgements

00:10:28.753 --> 00:10:33.215
in 1994 and 1995, Swift got to work

00:10:33.215 --> 00:10:39.180
and started assessing what
things they could try to claim.

00:10:39.180 --> 00:10:40.514
This was very challenging in part

00:10:40.514 --> 00:10:43.225
because the Philippines' courts

00:10:43.225 --> 00:10:45.353
did not recognize the U.S. judgment,

00:10:45.353 --> 00:10:49.649
and so they couldn't go after
any assets in the Philippines.

00:10:49.649 --> 00:10:51.734
They had to go after assets elsewhere.

00:10:51.734 --> 00:10:54.445
In effect, I was limited to executing

00:10:54.445 --> 00:10:58.074
on whatever Marcos' assets
were in the United States,

00:10:58.074 --> 00:11:00.785
and of course, the
Marcoses weren't willing

00:11:00.785 --> 00:11:03.829
to testify as to that.

00:11:03.829 --> 00:11:06.499
I took their depositions several times,

00:11:06.499 --> 00:11:09.794
and they claimed they
didn't know anything.

00:11:11.796 --> 00:11:13.255
Of course, that was false.

00:11:22.431 --> 00:11:24.475
So the turning point as it relates

00:11:24.475 --> 00:11:28.437
to collections was between 2000 and 2010.

00:11:28.437 --> 00:11:30.564
And essentially, what happened was there

00:11:30.564 --> 00:11:35.569
was an oil investor in Texas
by the name of Alan Meeker,

00:11:35.903 --> 00:11:39.448
and he found some
attractive parcels of land

00:11:39.448 --> 00:11:41.617
that he was interested in purchasing.

00:11:41.617 --> 00:11:43.869
But for the life of him,
the way that he describes it

00:11:43.869 --> 00:11:45.913
was he couldn't find the darn owner.

00:11:46.956 --> 00:11:50.167
And as he was doing due
diligence on this land,

00:11:50.167 --> 00:11:55.172
he remembered a rumor that he
had heard when he was younger

00:11:55.339 --> 00:11:59.135
that Ferdinand Marcos had
actually purchased a bunch

00:11:59.135 --> 00:12:01.929
of oil producing lands in Texas.

00:12:01.929 --> 00:12:04.432
These lands proved to be very valuable

00:12:04.432 --> 00:12:08.352
and ultimately was able
to settle that litigation

00:12:08.352 --> 00:12:10.062
for $10 million.

00:12:10.062 --> 00:12:13.107
So Swift was absolutely overjoyed

00:12:13.107 --> 00:12:15.860
at the prospect of finally
having enough money

00:12:15.860 --> 00:12:18.112
to distribute to the class members

00:12:18.112 --> 00:12:20.865
who had waited for so many decades

00:12:20.865 --> 00:12:23.701
to see anything after the judgements came.

00:12:24.994 --> 00:12:28.456
But the challenges were
still very great in terms

00:12:28.456 --> 00:12:32.168
of how the money would
actually get distributed.

00:12:32.168 --> 00:12:37.089
So while I had 10,000
checks with names on them,

00:12:37.089 --> 00:12:38.591
many of the people had died.

00:12:38.591 --> 00:12:42.178
By that, I mean more than 20%.

00:12:42.178 --> 00:12:47.183
So the process was
laborious and much slower

00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:50.686
than I would've liked,
but it was very effective,

00:12:50.686 --> 00:12:53.105
and it was also gratifying.

00:12:55.065 --> 00:13:00.070
The faces of the people
expressing their gratitude

00:13:00.696 --> 00:13:05.034
were enough of a reward that I felt good

00:13:05.034 --> 00:13:06.952
about what we were doing,

00:13:06.952 --> 00:13:11.499
and I knew that it was gonna benefit them.

00:13:11.499 --> 00:13:15.503
I would often ask people
frequently through an interpreter,

00:13:15.503 --> 00:13:18.047
"How are you going to use the money?"

00:13:18.047 --> 00:13:22.802
And I was told that they would use it

00:13:22.802 --> 00:13:27.807
to put a cemetery stone by the
church for their loved one,

00:13:30.267 --> 00:13:33.604
or they would send their
children to school,

00:13:33.604 --> 00:13:35.731
or they would simply buy food.

00:13:35.731 --> 00:13:39.276
The older people would use the money

00:13:39.276 --> 00:13:41.445
to buy prescription drugs

00:13:41.445 --> 00:13:43.322
that they couldn't otherwise afford.

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:57.711
10 years, I'm starting to rise again.

00:13:57.711 --> 00:14:02.716
Now like a phoenix,
hopefully, the truth will come

00:14:03.551 --> 00:14:06.554
from the ashes of what was done to us.

00:14:08.973 --> 00:14:11.892
Ferdinand Marcos and
his family were exiled

00:14:11.892 --> 00:14:14.854
from the Philippines in the 1980s,

00:14:14.854 --> 00:14:18.983
but subsequent to his death,
they were allowed to return.

00:14:18.983 --> 00:14:21.735
And since then, they have managed

00:14:21.735 --> 00:14:24.154
to really regain the popularity

00:14:24.154 --> 00:14:28.075
that they enjoyed during his term.

00:14:28.075 --> 00:14:31.287
Congratulations, Senator Imee Marcos.

00:14:33.497 --> 00:14:35.040
Well, it's outrageous

00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:40.045
that the nation allows this to happen.

00:14:40.296 --> 00:14:43.632
Will I say sorry for the power generation?

00:14:43.632 --> 00:14:46.886
Will I say sorry for the
highest literacy rate in Asia?

00:14:47.761 --> 00:14:49.221
What am I to say sorry about?

00:14:50.180 --> 00:14:53.183
In the Philippines, as in other countries,

00:14:53.183 --> 00:14:55.978
elections are frequently won by those

00:14:55.978 --> 00:15:00.983
who can more readily distribute money

00:15:01.317 --> 00:15:03.819
during the election process.

00:15:03.819 --> 00:15:08.824
The Marcoses have had access
to the monies acquired

00:15:09.283 --> 00:15:11.660
and hidden by Ferdinand Marcos.

00:15:11.660 --> 00:15:12.494
The richest

00:15:12.494 --> 00:15:14.705
is Senator Ferdinand Marcos, Jr.,

00:15:14.705 --> 00:15:18.375
who declared a net worth of
more than 400 million pesos.

00:15:20.502 --> 00:15:24.089
Bongbong Marcos, his son,
is running for president

00:15:24.089 --> 00:15:27.468
in 2022 and is polling quite well.

00:15:30.346 --> 00:15:33.807
I'm confident that some of the money

00:15:33.807 --> 00:15:38.187
that was acquired by Ferdinand
Marcos and hidden is going

00:15:38.187 --> 00:15:44.318
to find its way into the 2022
election in the Philippines.

